  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Field Card",
    "overview": "SafeHaven should feel like the calm instruction card in a go-bag: plain words, big readable buttons, and nothing to decode. Anyone (a child, a grandparent, someone shaking and in the dark) should be able to read the screen and tap the right thing on the first try. The interface is quiet on purpose, so that when something does turn red it is unmistakable.\n\n**Dark is the default.** Surfaces are a soft neutral grey with near-white text. Light mode, chosen in First aid › Appearance or by \"Match phone\", is a warm beige with dark-brown text. Pure white is not used anywhere. Every action is a real button: a rounded 56pt shape with an icon and a short verb label. The interface uses no boxed \"cards\", no dashboard metrics and no decorative rules. Grouping comes from spacing and simple section headings.\n\nUrgency still escalates in visible steps (the **urgency ladder**): Watch is an amber header, Warning a red header, and Emergency the whole screen in red. Haptics follow the level: one light tap, then two heavy pulses, then repeating pulses until the user acts.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark grey by default, warm beige in light mode, never pure white.",
      "Real buttons: rounded (12px), at least 56pt tall, icon plus a verb label, centered.",
      "Three button kinds: filled (one main action), tonal (everything else), plain text (cancel and leave).",
